 "title": "Low-power Schmitt trigger",
 "source": {
  "revision": "",
  "pages": 6
 },
 "summary": "A single non-inverting buffer with a Schmitt-trigger input and an open-drain output, in a five-lead SOT23-5. It runs from 0.8 V to 3.6 V, accepts inputs up to 3.6 V, and draws at most 0.5 µA standing current. Ioff circuitry suits it to partial power-down use. Open-drain outputs of several parts can be tied together to make an active-LOW wired-OR or an active-HIGH wired-AND.",
